  "metadata_synthesis": "Kiyoshi Kurosawa's 1997 psychological horror masterpiece. The true progenitor of the J-horror boom. A chilling, hypnotic police procedural.",
  "setting_and_subculture": "Late 90s Tokyo. Sterile interrogation rooms. Empty beaches. Dilapidated hospitals. A city composed entirely of corpses and liminal spaces.",
  "visual_tone_and_feel": "Unflinchingly stark. Lingering wide shots. Ordinary objects transformed into terrifying totems. A visual descent into total madness.",
  "media_era_tone": "Pre-millennial Japanese dread. The quiet dawn of J-horror. Deep societal malaise masked by mundane routines. Cinematic mesmerism.",
  "pacing_and_structure": "A slow, deliberate poisoning. Procedural pushed into obsession. Hypnotic and circular. A creeping infection of the mind.",
  "atmosphere_and_mood": "Unbearably disquieting. Cold, clinical, and empty. A howling void of meaning. Deeply scarring. A pervasive sense of inevitable doom.",
  "themes_and_messages": "The fragile illusion of sanity. The infectious nature of evil. Repressed societal rage bursting forth. The terrifying emptiness of modern life.",
  "character_relationships": "A tragic game of cat and mouse. The blurring line between investigator and monster. A dying marriage shadowed by illness. Contagious psychosis.",
  "lead_character_type": "An obsessive, unraveling detective. A mesmerizing, amnesiac drifter acting as an empty vessel. Ordinary people turned spontaneous killers.",
  "story_and_plot_type": "Psychological thriller. Contagion horror. Existential police procedural. A slow descent into the abyss.",
  "who_and_when": "A burnt-out detective and an empty drifter. Tokyo. 1997. An era on the brink of an invisible, spiritual collapse.",
  "emotional_evocation": "Deep, lingering unease. An icy chill down the spine. Profound existential terror. The terrifying realization that anyone could snap."
